{
"lines": [
{
"text": "Your phone never talks to GPS satellites.",
"start": 0.35,
"end": 3.034
},
{
"text": "It only listens.",
"start": 3.284,
"end": 4.353
},
{
"text": "About thirty GPS satellites circle the Earth, twenty thousand kilometres up.",
"start": 4.803,
"end": 9.641
},
{
"text": "Each one carries an atomic clock, and keeps broadcasting two things: the exact time, and where it is.",
"start": 9.991,
"end": 16.277
},
{
"text": "That signal takes about seven hundredths of a second to reach you.",
"start": 16.627,
"end": 20.017
},
{
"text": "Your phone times that delay from at least four satellites, and turns each one into a distance.",
"start": 20.367,
"end": 25.773
},
{
"text": "Only one spot on Earth fits every distance.",
"start": 26.073,
"end": 28.526
},
{
"text": "That's you. Accurate to about five metres, without ever saying a word.",
"start": 28.676,
"end": 32.77
}
],
